# Arguments for the MicroMound daemon (read by micromound.service). One line; edit and
# `sudo systemctl restart micromound`. Run `/opt/micromound/micromound` with no arguments for the
# full list. State lives in /var/lib/micromound (identity, durable state, evidence).
#
# --hardware      drive REAL ports (GPIO character device + ADS1115 over I2C). Without it every port
#                 is in-memory and a manifest naming physical ports is refused unless --simulate.
# --controller    the ANTHILL base URL (https only). Omit to run offline.
# --enroll-token  the one-time token ANTHILL minted for THIS mound id; used once, then ignored.
# --tier          edge_queen (a Pi running the full colony; default) or deterministic_controller.
#
MICROMOUND_ARGS=--manifest /etc/micromound/manifest.json --hardware --state /var/lib/micromound --controller https://anthill.example --enroll-token REPLACE-ME
